In the original ordered primary coordinates its matrix is
\[
 C_{(a,b),(i,j)}
 =\begin{cases}
 a_{i-a,j-b},&0\le i-a,j-b\le8,\\
 0,&\text{otherwise}.
 \end{cases}
 \qquad C\in\operatorname{Mat}_{q'\times q}(\mathbb C).
 \tag{CEP4}
\]
Evaluation of CEP2 proves this entry formula, including its absence
